senses.gloss:
अपकर्ष m. drawing away, taking off, diminution,
deterioration;
 anticipation (ph.).

अपचारिन् a. deviating from (—˚);
 acting improperly;
faithless, false, adulterous.

अ॑पचिति f. expiation, vengeance for (gen.);
 awe, honour,
respect.

अ॑पथ n. no or the wrong road;
 fig. a bad course or wrong
place.

अपभ्रंश॑ m. falling down;
 fallen off, i.e. corrupted
or vulgar language.

1 अ॑पर a. hinder, farther, later, inferior, posterior,
western;
 following (in sp. & t.);
 different from, another than (abl. or
gen.), foreign (opp. स्व), particular, strange, extraordinary. m.
अपर hind-foot of an elephant. n. अ॑परम् adv. in future (also
अपर॑म्);
 further, moreover (±च);
 west of (abl.). अ॑परेण
behind, west of (acc.).

अपरक्त a. discoloured, pale;
 averse from (abl.),
unfavourable.

अ॑पराद्ध a. sinned;
 having sinned, guilty. n. impers.
it has been sinned by (instr.), against (gen. or loc.);
 as subst. = seq.

अपरान्त m. last end, death;
 the farthest west, pl. its
inhabitants.

अपरिक्लिष्ट a. not vexed or troubled;
 ˚पूर्व not
vexed before.

1 अपरिग्रह m. non-comprehension, non-acceptance;
 want
of property.

अपरिहीयमान a. unavoided;
 ˚नं कृ carry out,
accomplish.

अपरोक्ष a. not beyond the eye or out of sight,
witnessed, testified, perceptible, clear;
 abstr. अपरोक्ष++˚त्व n. —
अपरो˚क्षम् & अपरो˚क्षे in the presence of;
 अ॑परोक्षात् clearly.

अपर्व॑न् n. no joint (Ved. loc. the same form);
 no Parvan-
or holiday (v. प॑र्वन्).

अपविद्ध a. pierced, hit;
 thrown away, rejected,
removed, given up, neglected.

2 अपश्चिम a. the last of all (lit. h. no last);
 n. adv.
last of all.

अपसद m. an outcast;
 a. base-born (of a father inferior
to the mother), low, vile (esp. —˚).

अपहार m. taking away, stealing, robbing, concealing;
 a.
अपहा˚रक & अपहा˚रिन्.

अपान॑ m. the wind that goes downward (in the body);
 the
anus.

आपन्न a. having got or come to (˚— or —˚);
 unfortunate,
unhappy.

अपाय m. departure (a. ˚यिन्);
 going astray or missing the
aim, i.e. disadvantage, danger, diminution, loss;
 end, death.

अपाश्रय m. support, refuge;
 p. अपाश्रय++˚वन्त् &
अपाशय˚यिन्.

आपात m. rushing on, onset, entering into (—˚);
 sudden
event. ˚— or ˚तस् adv. immediately, at first sight.
